{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '950,1015p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1260,1400p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; sed -n '1,180p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; git diff --stat master...HEAD; rg -n 'satisfies\\\\?|memoize|binding|assoc nil|unary|private|for.*seq' docs/agents/build-n-test.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '950,1015p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1260,1400p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; sed -n '1,180p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; git diff --stat master...HEAD; rg -n 'satisfies\\\\?|memoize|binding|assoc nil|unary|private|for.*seq' docs/agents/build-n-test.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md\"","aggregated_output":"(defn decode\n  \"Validate and expand a row pack, including canonical cursor-cell numbering.\n   For task roots, run X1 and frame validation after numbering.\"\n  ([wire] (decode* wire default-budget))\n  ([wire budget] (decode* wire (dissoc budget :check-numbering))))\n\n\n(defn canonical-under\n  \"Test-only §5.5 re-emission under an explicit stream correspondence.\n   Missing marker coverage fails; neither traversal order nor original\n   cursor-cell numbering chooses a logical identity. Accepts a carrier.\"\n  [wire correspondence]\n  (let [task (decode* wire (assoc default-budget :check-numbering false))]\n    (letfn [(rewrite-slot\n              [d x]\n              (cond (ref? d) (rewrite x) (refs? d) (mapv rewrite x)\n                    (and (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d) (= :row (first x))) [:row (rewrite (second x))]\n                    :else x))\n            (rewrite\n              [n]\n              (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n                (if (= :stream kind)\n                  (let [id (first slots)]\n                    (when-not (contains? correspondence id) (bad! :missing-stream-correspondence [id]))\n                    (node :stream [(get correspondence id) (get correspondence id)]))\n                  (node kind (mapv rewrite-slot (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n      (emit (rewrite task)))))\n\n\n(defn- value-node\n  [x]\n  (check-literal-markers! x)\n  [:lit x])\n\n\n(defn- decoded-value\n  [v]\n  (case (first v)\n    :row {:yin.k/row (second v)}\n    :cursor-cell {:yin.k/cursor-cell (second v)}\n    :lit (if (marker-shaped? (second v)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :marker []) (second v))))\n\n\n(defn- keyed-node\n  [kind m encode]\n  (node kind (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (encode v)]) m)))\n\n\n(defn- env-node\n  [e encode]\n  (node :env [(keyed-node :bindings (:yin.k/bindings e) encode) (:yin.k/store-of e)]))\n\n\n(defn- kframe-node\n  [f encode]\n  (node :kframe [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\n                 (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) (:yin.k/rd f)]))\n\n\n(def pending-keys\n  {:next [:yin.k/cursor-cell]\n   :put [:yin.k/stream :yin.k/value :yin.k/op-id]\n   :ffi [:yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/call-id :yin.k/op]\n   :ffi-request [:yin.k/call-id :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/response-cursor-cell :yin.k/op-id]\n   :link-request [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/op-id]\n   :link-response [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell]\n\n### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n\n**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\ntail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\nsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\neffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\ntruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\nsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\ngreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\nlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n6b, 6c-pre.\n\n**Acceptance (6c).**\n\n1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n   tail boundaries `[]`.\n3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n    segment under `canonical-under`.\n11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n\n**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\ncarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\ndocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\neach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\nobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\nrow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\nretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n\n### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\nnot edited.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Verification honesty\n\n- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5)` on the worked\n  example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`). The\n  stack slices `[f]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and at `(g)` in\n  `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived twice from the §4.3 walk and agreed\n  with the reviewer's derivation; the register `phys(1) = 0`, `phys(2) =\n  3` follow from phase-5 §6.3 row 2, whose pinned `live` at pc 3 is `[0]`\n  (`{T0,T3}` minus the destination `T3`), the same set §4.2 step 4 and\n  §5.6 item 3 compute by subtracting the virtual `rd 2` before mapping.\n  The multi-frame bases in 6c item 6 (`2, 4` for the expression alone;\n  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\n  twice from the kernel's call arm (`stack.cljc:716-733`, base = height\n  after popping callee and operands); the first pass forgot the pushed\n  operator, and revision 2's lowering rule used the height **before**\n  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n  partition the stack (item 9).\n- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n  exists.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n    v))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n  :semantic-register)\n\n\n(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- composition\n  [opts]\n  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n          :modules stream-modules}\n         opts))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-opts\n  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n  [opts]\n  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n\n\n(defn machine\n  ([] (machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (case *lane*\n     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n\n\n(defn lane-of\n  [m]\n  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n          :else :semantic-register)))\n\n\n(def segment-of\n  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n  (memoize layout/segment))\n\n\n(defn kernel-space\n  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k holds.\"\n  [k]\n  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @code-index))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-load\n  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n  [k v]\n  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n        sg (segment-of v)\n        k (if (= :stack kind)\n            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n    (if (= :stack kind)\n      (assoc k :stack [])\n      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n\n\n(defn load-program\n  [m ast]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n\n\n(defn lane-closure\n  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n  [m c]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  []\n  {:source-index @source-index})\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn cat-of\n  [p q]\n  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n\n\n(defn with-cat\n  [ast]\n  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc      | 898 +++++++++++++++++++++\n test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc     | 425 ++++++++++\n .../semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc  | 405 +++++++++-\n 3 files changed, 1715 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:230:#   (binding [clojure.test/*test-out* (java.io.StringWriter.)] (clojure.test/test-vars [v]))\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:154:  merged under the lexical chain's bindings (§4.4), and a de Bruijn\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:166: :yin.k/env   {:yin.k/bindings {sym V …} :yin.k/store-of M?}\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:249:| `:env` | `bindings-cref  store-of` | unchanged (draft §5.1) |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:250:| `:bindings` | `S₁ V₁  S₂ V₂ …` sorted by symbol | unchanged |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:252:`:window`, `:bindings`, `:store` and every other tabled keyed row are\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:302:   free-env-cref    ; NEW: a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (§6.3)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:385:| S4 | every `:yin.k/env` present is `{:yin.k/bindings {S V …}}` optionally with `:yin.k/store-of M`; `:yin.k/deliver` is a map | `:env-shape` / `:deliver-shape` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:424:| E1 | no binding key is reserved (`vm/reserved-name?`) | `:reserved-name` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:425:| E2 | **`E` is the free environment under the lexical chain.** With `C = (set (mapcat params (chain (body pc))))` the lexically bound names at that pc (a return frame's chain is that of its own `pc`): (a) **every name of `C` is a key of `bindings`**, a nil binding being a present key (`bind-params` nil-fills, so a lexical name is never absent; an absent one would be nil-filled on lower and break the canonical round trip); (b) `(apply dissoc bindings C) = (apply dissoc (:free-env task) C)` as maps of `V`: a key outside `C` the free environment lacks, a free key `E` lacks, or a differing value, is a defect | `:free-env-mismatch` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:431:| X1 | the root's `free-env` decodes to a map `{S V …}` with symbol keys, sorted and unique on the wire, none reserved (`vm/reserved-name?`, the same check `create-vm` runs on its `:env`, `vm/check-bindings!`, `vm.cljc:161-168`); it is the `:free-env` every E2 compares against | `:free-env-shape` / `:reserved-name` (path `[:free-env]`) |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:760:design. The free bindings that *are* observable, by any closure's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:774:context; it never runs code, never fills a binding from the receiver's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:869:binding `y` in the act's `E` changed to `8` → `:free-env-mismatch`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:936:their members' keys, and `:store`, `:bindings` and the parked table in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:999:slot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1018:  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1032:Merkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1033:`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1201:    2-cycle with the same reserved-name binding, carried by\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1297:   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1315:   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1374:  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1485:\"the saved window's values, the environment's bindings and the depth of\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1743:2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:1756:8. **Sorted keys.** Window and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
